  "body": "What happens: on upstream main 3f6ecb4a, `cargo test -p xtask -- no_gate_map_names_a_moved_module_as_app` fails (so every `cargo xtask gate quick` that touches `xtask/` is red):\n\n```\nGate maps naming moved modules as app::<module>: [\"altmill_machines: app::post\", \"doosan_dnm_a_state: app::post\", \"lathe_post_inch: app::post\", \"program_units: app::post\", \"rotary_feed_cap: app::post\", \"thread_boss: app::machining2d\", \"thread_boss: app::drilling\", \"thread_mill: app::tools\", \"thread_mill: app::machining2d\", \"thread_passes: app::machining2d\"]\n```\n\nExpected: those suites' `Gate map` header lines name the crates the modules moved to (e.g. `camcraft-post`, not `app::post`), so the test passes.\n\nEvidence: reproduced on a clean worktree of upstream/main 3f6ecb4a (no local changes), xtask/src/gate_maps_tests.rs:107. Found while working #1413.\n\nDone means: the ten gate-map headers are corrected and `cargo test -p xtask` is green on main.\n",
